    "reviewedOn": "2026-09-18",
    "checks": [
      {
        "claim": "NAMED_ITEM_NOT_EQUIPPED_IS_BACKGROUND",
        "search": "use_item_t constructor, engine/player/player.cpp",
        "finding": "`item = player->find_item_by_name( item_name ); if ( !item ) { background = true; return; }` (player.cpp:9874-9884). A named item the actor does not equip yields a background action, and `select_action` skips background actions before any readiness or condition check (player.cpp:14229-14230)."
      },
      {
        "claim": "SLOT_WITHOUT_ON_USE_EFFECT_IS_BACKGROUND",
        "search": "use_item_t::init and use_items_t::init, engine/player/player.cpp",
        "finding": "`use_item_t::init` looks up `special_effect( SPECIAL_EFFECT_SOURCE_NONE, SPECIAL_EFFECT_USE )` and, with neither buff nor action created, sets `background = true` and erases the entry from the foreground action list (player.cpp:10024-10029). `use_items_t::init` sets `background = true` when no sub-actions were created at all (player.cpp:10285-10290)."
      },
      {
        "claim": "USE_ITEMS_PARENT_IS_THE_FOREGROUND_ENTRY",
        "search": "use_items_t::ready and create_use_subactions, engine/player/player.cpp",
        "finding": "`use_items_t` is the object in the APL's foreground action list; its generated `use_item` sub-actions are internal. `ready()` returns true only when at least one sub-action is ready (player.cpp:10295-10312). Authority identity therefore remains the `use_items` entry."
      },
      {
        "claim": "INDIVIDUAL_COOLDOWN_COMES_FROM_THE_EFFECT_DRIVER_SPELL",
        "search": "special_effect_t::cooldown, engine/item/special_effect.cpp:745-765",
        "finding": "With no explicit override and an item-effect row whose `cooldown_duration` is -1, the lookup falls through to `driver()->cooldown()` — the effect spell's own `_cooldown`."
      },
      {
        "claim": "READY_CHECKS_INDIVIDUAL_AND_GROUP_COOLDOWNS_DIFFERENTLY",
        "search": "use_item_t::ready, engine/player/player.cpp",
        "finding": "The shared group is checked with a strict `cooldown_group->remains() > 0`, while the item's own cooldown goes through `action_t::ready()` and therefore `cooldown_t::is_ready()`, which allows queueing within the player's cooldown tolerance. The two rules are NOT the same and must not share a bridge."
      }
    ]
  },
